<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:bml="org.blockml.bml.annotation.BmlAnnotation"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation"
  xmlns:ex="org.blockml.bml.exception"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <name>Text</name>
  <type>type:Text</type>
  <baseType>type:PrimitiveType</baseType>
  <is>A text string</is>

  <documentation>BOM Core primitive ValueType for text. Unqualified name Text resolves to
    org.blockml.bml.type.Text. Replaces the former String type — BlockML describes semantic types, not
    implementation data structures. Renderers may map Text to Java String, TypeScript string,
    Python str, C# string, or any target representation.

    Semantic subtypes extend Text: TypeIdentifier / TypeReference, PackageIdentifier /
    PackageReference, InstanceIdentifier / InstanceReference, MemberIdentifier (PropertyIdentifier /
    PropertyReference / …), Version, URL, URI, UUID, FilePath, MimeType, …
    Concrete payload values are stored on Properties — not on the Text type itself.

    Member values of this type may contain restricted ${ } holes in running text
    (InterpolatedTextValue). A whole-value "${ expr }" remains an ExpressionValue. See
    doc:Expressions.

    Optional configuration Properties (minLength, maxLength) configure a Property's owned Text
    instance via inline type syntax — Text{maxLength: 100}. Positional order: minLength, maxLength.
    See 20_value_type_instance_configuration.md.</documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="doc:Expressions" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Interpolated Text holes, #this lookup, and Restricted Profile.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:ValueTypeParsing" relation="SeeAlso">
      parseValue identity — every authored string is Text.
    </see>
  </references>
  <capabilities>
    <parseValue
      override="true"
      abstract="false"
      type="Transformation"
      inputType="Text"
      outputType="bml:Self">
      <documentation>
        Identity — every authored string is a Text value. Length bounds are instance
        configuration (minLength / maxLength), applied after parse.
      </documentation>
      <throws>
        <ex:InvalidValueException />
      </throws>
      <implementation language="TypeScript"><![CDATA[
        (raw: string): string => raw
      ]]></implementation>
    </parseValue>
  </capabilities>
  <properties>
    <minLength type="Integer">
      <documentation>Minimum allowed text length (inclusive). Configured via Text{minLength: n}.</documentation>
    </minLength>
    <maxLength type="Integer">
      <documentation>Maximum allowed text length (inclusive). Configured via Text{maxLength: n}.</documentation>
    </maxLength>
  </properties>
</block>
